    "This proves the format, not the cryptography: vectors show that the specified bytes are produced and refused, not that the primitives are sound, that the implementation is side-channel free, or that it is safe to use. HIDE is experimental and unaudited.",
    "Nothing here checks an implementation's own writers, only its readers: every vector is an input, and the harness never asks a command to encrypt.",
    "detached-signature vectors are hash-checked only. spec §14 makes the detached-signature file implementation-defined and conformance/vectors/README.md obliges only the recorded hash; byte-for-byte reproduction is pinned by `cargo test -p hide-sign --test vectors`.",
    "The transient behaviour the vectors cannot express: memory bounds before allocation (only the refusal of rejections/argon2-memory.test-secret is observed), timing, and running as a service.",
    "Conformance is claimed against a specific manifestSha256. A different vector set needs a different claim."
